WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.167
- It's the first of the month.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.502
You know what that means:

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:03.603
Rent’s due.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:07.974
- [Offscreen voice 1:] Oh, my God! [Laughing]
- [Offscreen voice 2:] Oh, wow.

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:10.010
- [Offscreen voice 3:] Thank you.
- [Offscreen voice 2:] Thank you so much.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:11.211
- What's up, guys?

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.512
I'm Tyrann Mathieu, also

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.613
known as The Landlord.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.848
They call me The Landlord

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.616
cuz I own the field and I take care of

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.818
Chiefs kingdom, but right now my social

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.620
responsibility goes much beyond that.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:21.988
A lot of people have been

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.524
impacted by COVID-19, especially

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.892
in my hometown of New Orleans.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.794
I'm hoping to find a few families

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.962
that I can really impact

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.630
and help and love and support.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.098
I'm looking forward to checking them out.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:39.973
- Hi, Tyrann.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:41.274
My name's Sarah Jane, and I'm a

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.742
unit director here at the Boys &amp;

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.544
Girls Clubs of Southeast Louisiana.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.112
And I'd love to introduce you to

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.414
one of our families that's been

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.516
affected by the COVID-19 virus.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:50.817
We've got Marcus, one

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:51.818
of our youngest members, and his mother,

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:54.521
Torri, who is a health care worker who has

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.389
recently gotten off of quarantine due

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.291
to exhibiting symptoms with the virus.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.060
Um, they're an amazing family to

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.294
have with us, and I'd love for

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.429
you to get to know them more.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.435
- Hey. Can you hear me?

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.203
- Hi, Tyrann. How you doing?

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.771
- Hey! How you doing?

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:15.508
- I can’t complain. I can’t complain.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.776
- I've heard so many great things

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.678
about you and your son, Marcus.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.681
- I hope that he’s doing well.
- Yes. Yes. Correct.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:21.948
- Yeah.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.216
Also, I've heard that you, that

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.851
you've recently recovered from COVID-19.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:28.221
- Yes.
- I’m so happy to hear that.

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:31.324
Um, I have a brother actually that's

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:34.060
a registered nurse, so I'm so grateful

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.528
for you being on the front line,

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.497
um, and for all that you do.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.432
Um, and I'm so happy that you're

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:42.469
back working too.
- I'm excited too.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.705
Trust me, the people I work for, they were excited too.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.273
- [Offscreen voice:] Yes, we were.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:51.144
- You heard my boss just said that?
[All laughing]

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.146
- So, hey, can I ask you, like, how was

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.715
it, how was it dealing with the, having

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.951
those symptoms and not being able to work?

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:58.718
How was that?

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.520
- It was lonely.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.623
That was, I think that was the most

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:07.160
difficult part, was being by myself.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.195
I don't think I would ever want

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.830
anybody to have to experience that.

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.332
Cuz you're basically,

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.634
you know, by yourself, just

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.069
hoping and praying everything

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:19.372
turns out well, you know?
- I'm so glad

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:20.874
that you, that you was able to recover

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:23.476
from that and that you seem to be in

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.944
great spirits right now, and that's

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.747
always a positive and, uh, I'm sure,

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.549
I'm sure Marcus, you know, was

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.117
there for you and I'm—so I don't want

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.519
you to ever feel like you're alone.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.020
Um, I want you to know that

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.355
I'm always with you too.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:39.592
- I appreciate that. I appreciate that, Tyrann.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.761
You are awesome.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.862
I have watched you

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:46.032
since high school at St. Augustine.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.635
- Aww.
- I’ve followed your career.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:51.905
So I want you to know that I have

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.540
rooted for you for a long time.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.842
I watched you go through your own trials

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:58.678
and tribulations, and I'm proud of you.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.280
I'm happy for you.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.750
And for me to see you win, that

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.418
made me feel like home wins too.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:06.753
You know?

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:07.220
- Yes, ma'am.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.555
I appreciate you so much.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.857
Hey, so I know Marcus is living

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:12.859
with his dad currently right now, right?

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.294
- Yeah.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.996
That's Marcus.
- How has

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.565
it been having him away?

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.201
- It has been difficult. Marcus is

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:23.636
my last little child.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.637
My other kids are

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:31.444
adults, so, trust me, it's been—I miss him. I miss him.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.178
- I bet.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.546
So I want to get personal

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.814
with you for just a moment.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.884
Uh, how was, how was the,

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.252
how was it financially for

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:41.154
you, not being able to work?

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.590
- Um, I'm basically trying to

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:47.160
recuperate from this situation.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.596
Normally, I'm able to go in and

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:52.098
work extra hours and stuff like that.

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:54.200
But, um, because I do normally

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.636
take care of one lady at her house,

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:59.239
to prevent from anything being,

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:05.545
you know, impeding upon her,
I have to take that into consideration.

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:09.249
- You know my nickname is 
The Landlord, uh, cuz, cuz, you

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:10.717
know, I take care of the field and,

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:12.485
uh, I take care of the kingdom too.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.754
And you deserve so much more, you

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.923
know, being a front-line worker, um,

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.725
you know, representing my hometown.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.827
Uh, you know, like I mentioned earlier,

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.495
my brother is a registered nurse as well.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.831
So I have, I have so much respect

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.566
for you guys and everything that

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:28.401
y'all do, everything y’all sacrifice,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.670
um, to really protect us.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.071
Um, but, but I want you to

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.206
check your phone right now.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.340
I want you to check your

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.209
texts for me, please, if you could.

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:37.644
- You are awesome.

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:40.480
I kid you not. This has been really awesome.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.416
- I've sent you one month’s rent,

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:45.885
and then my friends at Zelle, they're

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.754
actually gonna donate and match me.

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:49.088
So you're actually going to be covered

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.890
for two months. Check your account

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.792
once we hang up, and it should be there.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.061
- Just to have this conversation

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.863
with you was rewarding for me.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:57.530
Thank you.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.531
I'm so grateful.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:01.634
I appreciate the donation.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:02.869
I'm, I’m grateful.

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:03.336
I am.

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:03.870
I'm grateful.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.370
Thank you.

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:05.471
- Thank you so much.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:06.539
And you take care,

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:06.873
OK?

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:07.874
- I will.

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:08.474
You too.

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.243
And I'm gonna be watching you when

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.978
you do get to go back on the field, now.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:12.979
- I got you.

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:14.280
Thank you so much.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:14.814
- All right.

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:15.548
Thank you.

